/-
The SONNX shared Lean library — `Sonnx`.

This library holds the formalization vocabulary that every operator module
shares.  An operator module imports `Sonnx`, states its own relations over the
shared types, and is generated by the pipeline; it never redefines anything
from here.

* `Sonnx.Prelude`     — general list lemmas and the type-consistency predicate,
* `Sonnx.Tensor`      — the dense row-major tensor and its element access,
* `Sonnx.Broadcast`   — multidirectional (Numpy-style) broadcasting,
* `Sonnx.Index`       — the row-major enumeration of the indices of a shape,
* `Sonnx.Int`         — congruence modulo `2 ^ n`, the `n`-bit integer types,
                        and the wrap-around of an exact integer value,
* `Sonnx.Float`       — the floating-point values, formats and the
                        roundTiesToEven rounding relation,
* `Sonnx.Elementwise` — elementwise binary operations with broadcasting,
                        functional and relational.

Every declaration is in the `Sonnx` namespace; the module names are
`Sonnx.Tensor` and so on.  The library is Lean core only: no Mathlib.
-/
import Sonnx.Prelude
import Sonnx.Tensor
import Sonnx.Broadcast
import Sonnx.Index
import Sonnx.Int
import Sonnx.Float
import Sonnx.Elementwise
